# wtf

A small, fast CLI: **why did that last command fail (or succeed), and how do I fix it?**

`wtf` reads state captured by shell hooks at command time (command, exit code,
duration, cwd, git branch, and the actual output trace) and asks an LLM to explain
it in one or two sentences. `wtf fix` produces a corrected command, prints it,
and runs it after a y/N confirmation.

## Install

```sh
go build -o ~/.local/bin/wtf ./cmd/wtf
# zsh:
eval "$(wtf init zsh)"        # add this to ~/.zshrc
# bash:
eval "$(wtf init bash)"       # add this to ~/.bashrc
```

For exact output traces, either run inside [tmux](https://github.com/tmux/tmux)
(the hooks slice the pane history) or start a recorded shell:

```sh
wtf shell                     # runs $SHELL in a pty that tees all output
```

Run `wtf doctor` to verify hooks/providers.

## Commands

- `wtf` — did the last command succeed or fail, and why (1-2 sentences)
- `wtf explain` — same, in 2-3 sentences
- `wtf fix` — print the corrected command, then run it after y/N
- `wtf use [provider] [model]` — interactive picker (or set directly with args)
- `wtf init zsh|bash` — print the shell hooks for `eval`
- `wtf shell` — run your shell with full output recording
- `wtf doctor` — install/health check of providers and hooks
- `wtf version`

## Providers

Claude Code CLI (`claude -p --restricted`), Codex CLI (`codex exec`), OpenCode
(`opencode acp`, hand-rolled ACP/JSON-RPC client that walks nd-json on stdio),
and Ollama (`POST /api/chat` with `"stream":false`, models via `/api/tags`),
plus an in-memory `mock` for testing (`WTF_MOCK_RESPONSE="..." wtf --provider mock`).

```sh
wtf use                       # interactive provider + model picker
wtf use ollama qwen2.5-coder:7b
wtf --provider claude --model sonnet explain
```

Config lives in `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wtf/config.json` (`~/.config/wtf/config.json`).

## Brevity/enforcement

Model answers are clamped structurally (sentence caps + word caps, markdown/quote
stripping). Limits: status = 2 sentences/25 words, explain = 3 sentences/60 words,
fix = one line.

## Color

Colors respect `NO_COLOR` and non-TTY (piped) output via lipgloss.

## No Python

This project is Go only. Do not propose Python.
